#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/simulations_and_experiments/experiments-start-time.ipynb:77
msgid ""
"Let's start defining a model to illustrate this functionality, in this case "
"we choose the SPM"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/simulations_and_experiments/experiments-start-time.ipynb:-1
msgid "[2]:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/simulations_and_experiments/experiments-start-time.ipynb:-1
msgid "model = pybamm.lithium_ion.SPM()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/simulations_and_experiments/experiments-start-time.ipynb:98
msgid ""
"Usually we define an experiment such that each step is triggered when the "
"previous step is completed. For example, in this case we do a 1C discharge "
"for 20 minutes and then a C/3 charge for 10 minutes. The charge step starts "
"after 20 minutes, i.e. once the discharge step is finished."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/simulations_and_experiments/experiments-start-time.ipynb:-1
msgid "[3]:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/simulations_and_experiments/experiments-start-time.ipynb:-1
msgid ""
"experiment = pybamm.Experiment(\n"
"    [\"Discharge at 1C for 20 minutes\", \"Charge at C/3 for 10 minutes\"]\n"
")\n"
"sim = pybamm.Simulation(model, experiment=experiment)\n"
"sim.solve()\n"
"sim.plot()"
msgstr ""

